[0.05, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[29A\u001b[34;1m> 1. Add a concept of projects that set a working directory for the Antigravity harness.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m  2. I'm guessing workspaceOnly enables commands that are inside the sandbox. We should add UI that allows programs to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  be run that want to escape the sandbox, but only after review by the user.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m  3. Update README.md and add `/skills/` to `.gitignore`.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m\u25cb\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 3m 7s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial analysis suggests that the `workspaceOnly` setting within the observed package might c...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m\u25cf\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 5 files \u001b[37m(policy.dart, hooks.dart, capabilities.dart, +2)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[32m\u25cf\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(grep -rn \"workspaceOnly\\|enableSandbox\\|confirmRunCommand\\|disable_sandbox\\|DisableSandbox\\|sandbox\" /Users/...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m\u2026 12 more actions (9 reads, 3 commands) \u2026\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[32m\u25cf\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(README.md)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[33m\u25cf\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m 7 commands \u001b[37m(+2 \u00b7 strings ~/.antigravi... \u00d73 \u00b7 python"]
[0.0, "o", "3 -c ' with op... \u00d72)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n\u001b[33;1mCommand\u001b[m\n\u001b[53C\u001b[90m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37;1mRequesting permission for:\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m   python3 -c '\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m   with open(\"/Users/brett/.antigravity/bin/localharness\", \"rb\") as f:\u001b[m\n\u001b[64D\u001b[37m\u001b[1K data = f.read()\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m   import re\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m   \u22ef (7 lines hidden)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[1mRun this command?\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, run command\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. Yes, and always allow in this conversation for commands that start with 'python3 -c '\u001b[K\r\nwith open(\"/Users/brett/.antigravity/bin/localharness\", \"rb\") as f:...'\r\n  3. Yes, and always allow for commands that start with 'python3 -c '\u001b[K\r\nwith open(\"/Users/brett/.antigravity/bin/localharness\", \"rb\") as f:...' (Persist to settings.json)\r\n  4. No, cancel\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m\u2191/\u2193\u001b[90;22m Navigate \u00b7 \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend \u00b7 \u001b[94;1m"]
[0.0, "o", "ctrl+g\u001b[90;22m edit/expand command\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[21X\u001b[?2026l"]
[3.598, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[J\u001b[31A\u001b[5C\u001b[1K \u2022 \u001b[1mRecommendation\u001b[m: Explicitly pass an intended workspace directory (such as a dedicated app support/workspace\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K folder or user-selected directory) or, if this app is intended as a pure chat assistant without filesystem\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K access, disable built-in file tools via \u001b[94mCapabilitiesConfig(enabledTools: const [])\u001b[m.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mThread Title Locked In at Session Creation\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[41D\u2022 In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd4590c603d32f32f;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_repository.dart#L142-L157\u0007ChatRepository.getOrCreateSession\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94mbuildAgentConfig\u001b[m embeds \u001b[94mthreadTitle\u001b[m into \u001b[94mCustomSystemInstructions\u001b[m only\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K when the session is first created (\u001b[94m_sessions.putIfAbsent\u001b[m). That works well with the current auto-titling flow\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K (since auto-titling runs before the first message creates the session), but if thread renaming is ever added\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K later, the existing session's system instructions will ret"]
[0.0, "o", "ain the initial title.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mComposer State Shared Across Thread Switches\u001b[m\n\u001b[44D\u001b[1K \u2022 \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jke574019f330a822e;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/widgets/markdown_composer.dart#L27-L30\u0007MarkdownComposer\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 holds a single \u001b[94mTextEditingController\u001b[m not keyed by \u001b[94mactiveThreadId\u001b[m. If a user types a draft in\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K Thread A and clicks Thread B in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8015991529845862;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/widgets/thread_sidebar.dart\u0007ThreadSidebar\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, the unsent draft remains in the input box for Thread B.\r\n\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[60C\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> 1. Add a concept of projects that set a working directory for the Antigravity harness.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  2. I'm guessing workspaceOnly enables commands that are inside the sandbox. We should add UI that allows programs to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  be run that want to escape the sandbox, but only after review by the user.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  3. Update README.md and add `/skills/` to `.gitignore`.\u001b[m\u001b[K"]
